Z||000000||V8Fiero||05-11-2001||08:51 PM||||Alright!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P><BR>Ive flushed the system out THREE times with Prestone super flush. ( I did get alot of rust out) I know that I got ALL the air out of the system. Rebuilt 4 core radiator. Right amount of antifreeze/water mix. NEW coolant sensor so I know Im getting a pretty good reading.......<P>AND the G*D DAMN thing still runs in the 220 range......................<P>this is just idling with the fan on......<P>Any suggestions before I sell this piece of crap............<P>P.S. This is still the 84 V8<P>||||reg||8
Z||000001||V8Fiero||05-11-2001||09:36 PM||||Ok. <P>I have been reading a few posts on the subject of overheating etc.<P>I think I might be on the right track now. Does anyone know what degree the stock thermostat on a SBC is? When I bought mine I just asked for a thermostat for a SBC. Didnt even think about asking for a 190* or lower.<P>Im thinking a stock one is probably in the 210 range? My guage Im sure isnt that accurate.<P>Thanks<BR>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT-maniac||05-11-2001||09:38 PM||||Have you checked for crushed coolant lines underneath the car ?.My car was overheating and I found the supply line was crushed almost flat. I replaced it ( not fun as you have to drop the whole front suspension ) and  my car hasn't overheated since. Easy thing to check anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000003||V8Fiero||05-11-2001||11:52 PM||||:sitting on chair feeling like an ass:<P><BR>Well I thought that I checked the coolant lines good...........<P>Upon the fine tooth comb method......pass side tube just by the rear tire is twisted and crushed.....DAMN.....Im happy but....yet Im not....more work to do....<P>Thanks GT&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;I owe you one....where did you get your replacement from?<P>Scott||||reg||1
